## Tool Priority (TOKEN CRITICAL)

i: Cheapest tool that gets the answer. Escalate only when cheaper tools are insufficient.

**Cost ladder (cheapest → most expensive):**
Bash(git/grep) ≈ Grep/Glob < Read(targeted) < Read(full file) < multiple Reads < Explore/Agent/subagent

T: need specific lines → A: Grep -n pattern | !Read full file
T: need file list → A: Glob specific pattern | !Glob broad
T: need git changes → A: Bash(git diff {{BASE_BRANCH}}..HEAD --name-only) | !subagent | !Explore
T: need more context → A: ask user before reading files speculatively
T: considering Explore/Agent → A: inform user "Esto gastará ~3-5x más tokens. ¿Continúo?" | wait confirmation
{{STACK_TOOL_PRIORITY}}
